---
import LegalPage from "~/components/LegalPage.astro";
import { localeParams, useTranslations } from "~/i18n";
import { toLanguage } from "~/i18n/config";
import { SITE } from "~/data/site";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return localeParams();
}

const language = toLanguage(Astro.params.lang);
const t = useTranslations(language);
---

<LegalPage
  language={language}
  path="legal/terms"
  title={t("legal.terms")}
  metaTitle={t("legal.meta.terms")}
  description="The terms that apply to using the TenPrint Software website and licensing its macOS applications."
>
  <p>
    These terms apply to the <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong> website and to the licences we grant for
    {SITE.name} applications. Using the site or installing an application means you accept them.
  </p>

  <h2>Licence grant</h2>
  <p>
    When you install one of our applications you receive a non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to
    use it. A free application may be used without payment for personal and commercial purposes alike.
    A paid licence covers use on up to two Macs that you personally operate, unless a volume licence
    agreed in writing says otherwise.
  </p>
  <p>
    The licence is perpetual for the major version you purchased, and every update released within
    that major version is included at no extra cost.
  </p>

  <h2>What you may not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Resell, sublicense, rent, or redistribute the software or a licence key.</li>
    <li>Share a licence key publicly or with people outside your own two-Mac allowance.</li>
    <li>Reverse engineer the software except to the extent that applicable law expressly permits.</li>
    <li>Remove or alter copyright notices or licensing mechanisms.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may deactivate a licence key that is being distributed publicly or used well beyond its seat
    allowance. Where the misuse was not deliberate, we will contact you first.
  </p>

  <h2>Trials</h2>
  <p>
    Paid features may be evaluated for the trial period stated on the product page, with no feature
    withheld during the trial. When the trial ends the application continues to work; only the paid
    features stop until a licence key is entered. Your data, layouts, and settings are never deleted
    because a trial expired.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates and availability</h2>
  <p>
    We release updates at our own discretion and do not guarantee any particular release schedule.
    Downloads are served from each product's website; we aim to keep them available continuously but
    do not guarantee uninterrupted access. If we ever discontinue an application, we will announce it
    on its product page and will not disable copies you have already installed.
  </p>

  <h2>Warranty and liability</h2>
  <p>
    The software is provided as is. To the fullest extent permitted by law we disclaim implied
    warranties of merchantability and fitness for a particular purpose. Our total liability arising
    from the software or these terms is limited to the amount you actually paid for the licence in the
    twelve months before the claim.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms limits liability for death, personal injury, fraud, or anything else that
    cannot lawfully be limited. If you are a consumer in the European Union, your statutory rights
    remain unaffected.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of {SITE.country}. If you are a consumer, you keep the
    protection of the mandatory rules of the country where you live, and you may also use the European
    Commission's online dispute resolution platform.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We answer
    every message ourselves.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
